       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order, because the dose as written is unsafe.\n\nAcetaminophen 2000 mg three times daily is 6,000 mg/day. That is above the usual adult maximum of 4,000 mg/day, and some institutions cap it at 3,000 mg/day. A single 2000 mg dose is also double the usual maximum of 1,000 mg. This carries a real risk of hepatotoxicity, even with normal liver function.\n\nHere are some options that might match what you intended:\n- **1000 mg PO three times daily** (3,000 mg/day), a common conservative regimen.\n- **1000 mg PO four times daily** (4,000 mg/day), the standard maximum. Doses should be at least 6 hours apart, and you should count all other acetaminophen sources.\n- **650 mg PO every 6 hours** (2,600 mg/day).\n\nTell me which regimen you want, or confirm that 2000 mg was a typo, and I'll enter it right away. If you really do intend the original dose, I'd suggest checking with pharmacy or your attending first."
      }
     ],
